    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "As directed, report dated 16.03.2021 from the Judicial Magistrate, Ist Class, Kurukshetra, has been received as per which the parties had recorded 1 of 2 Neutral Citation No:=2023:PHHC:031214 CRM-M-1654-2021 [2] their statements before the Trial Court in terms of the compromise arrived at between them; only the petitioner is arrayed as the accused; respondent No.2 is the complainant;\nthe petitioner has not been declared a proclaimed offender and that the compromise is genuine.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1697,
      "end": 2178,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "16.03.2021",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 1723,
          "end": 1733
        },
        {
          "text": "Judicial Magistrate, Ist Class, Kurukshetra",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 1743,
          "end": 1786
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "Learned State counsel has no objection if the present petition is allowed.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 2179,
      "end": 2254,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "In view of the above, continuation of the proceedings in pursuance of the afore-referred FIR in which offences are not heinous as also the matter having been compromised, would be an abuse of the process of law and in terms of the law laid down by the Supreme Court in Narinder Singh vs State of Punjab (2014) 6 SCC 466, this Court deems it just and proper to allow the petition and resultantly quash FIR No.213 dated 28.05.2020 registered under Sections 420, 370 IPC and Section 24 of the Emigration Act, 1983 at Police Station Kurukshetra University, District Kurukshetra and all proceedings arising therefrom qua the petitioner.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2255,
      "end": 2888,
